00:49:40.440 --> 00:49:58.500
<v Carmen Delzell>Damn, hell, and god, were words that could never be used in my grandparents' house, never. "Nigger," though, that was a word nobody seemed to mind. The damn niggers were getting too big for their britches. They were getting sassy. And worst of all, they wanted to sit next to you on the bus and at the Woolworth's lunch counter.
<v Carmen Delzell>“该死、见鬼、上帝”，是在我祖父母家绝对不能用的词，绝对不能。不过，“黑鬼”这个词，没人介意。该死的黑鬼越来越狂妄了。他们变得没大没小。最糟糕的是，他们想在公共汽车上和伍尔沃斯午餐柜台旁坐在你身边。

00:49:58.500 --> 00:50:32.460
<v Carmen Delzell>I heard this kind of talk my whole life from my grandmother, but it didn't begin to sink in until we couldn't go to Ocean View Amusement Park any more, because they said niggers went there. Meanwhile, my father, who thought [? Tuesie ?] was crazy as a bedbug and I was just like her, was running for school board on a platform of integration of the Beaumont, Texas, school system. He and my mother joined the Unitarian church, which, according to my grandmother, were a bunch of heathens. And the tension between my two families became more apparent and terribly confusing for me.
<v Carmen Delzell>我一生中从祖母那里听过这种谈话，但直到我们不能再去海洋景观游乐园，因为据说黑鬼去那儿，我才开始意识到这一点。与此同时，认为图西像床虫一样疯狂而我像她的父亲，正在以博蒙特学区整合为纲领竞选教育委员会成员。他和母亲加入了唯一神教派教堂，据我祖母说，那是一群异教徒。我和两个家庭之间的紧张关系变得更加明显，让我感到极度困惑。

00:50:32.460 --> 00:50:43.310
<v Ira Glass>OK, well that is the story that you need to know before we could bring you this latest installment from Carmen's life. Carmen's now back in Texas. And she put this story together with radio producer Jay Allison.
<v Ira Glass>好了，这就是在把卡门生活的最新片段带给你之前，你需要知道的故事。卡门现在回到了德克萨斯州。她和广播制作人杰·艾利森一起制作了这个故事。

