<v Carmen Delzell>That's EZ Malone from Currituck, North Carolina. My daughter and I were lucky enough to meet him in a junk store on our way home from my grandmother's funeral. EZ was looking for an electric frying pan. We weren't looking for anything in particular, until he looked at us and said "Hah." And that's when I realized we'd been looking for him.
<v Carmen Delzell>那是来自北卡罗来纳州科里塔克的埃兹·马隆。我和女儿很幸运，在从祖母葬礼回家的路上在一家旧货店遇到了他。埃兹在找电煎锅。我们没什么特别要找的，直到他看着我们说“哈”。就在那时我意识到我们一直在找他。

00:51:42.280 --> 00:52:12.550
<v Carmen Delzell>He said he'd been homeless a few years ago in New York City, until he met his girlfriend, Phyllis. She got him to move back to North Carolina, and they brought along her brain-damaged sister, who laughs all the time. And they all live together in a rented trailer. It's not so clear how they make a living. Sometimes, EZ gets a gig at a place called Fishbone's, down the road in a town called Duck.
<v Carmen Delzell>他说他几年前在纽约市无家可归，直到遇到了女朋友菲利斯。她让他搬回北卡罗来纳，他们还带上了她那个总是笑个不停、脑损伤的妹妹。他们全都住在一辆出租拖车里。他们怎么维持生计不太清楚。有时候，埃兹会在鸭镇路边的鱼骨餐馆找到演出机会。

00:52:12.550 --> 00:52:29.490
<v Carmen Delzell>He told us he could play the guitar his teeth and his feet. But it was the way he talked that convinced us to invite him to my son's place for supper. We never could have done if my grandmother was in the car. She was afraid of black men. But since she was dead, I figured it was OK.
<v Carmen Delzell>他告诉我们他能用牙齿和脚弹吉他。但正是他说话的方式让我们决定邀请他到我儿子家吃晚饭。如果我祖母在车里，我们绝不可能这样做。她害怕黑人。但既然她去世了，我想应该没问题。

00:52:29.490 --> 00:52:58.640
<v Ez Malone>Now I'll tell you, it all started in church, when I used to go to church with my father years ago. He was a minister, by the way. So when I was just a lad, my father told me, he said, "I'm going to buy you a guitar." And being so young, I took it for a joke. Time passed, and he actually bought me a guitar. So there I was, late at night, all times of night, just bamming on the guitar. I wasn't making no sense with the thing, just--
<v Ez Malone>现在我告诉你，这一切都始于教堂，多年前我常和父亲去教堂。顺便说一下，他是位牧师。当我还是个孩子时，父亲告诉我，他说：“我要给你买把吉他。”我当时太小，以为他在开玩笑。时间流逝，他真的给我买了一把吉他。于是我深夜，整晚都在拨弄吉他。我根本搞不懂那玩意儿，只是——

00:52:58.640 --> 00:52:59.080
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:52:59.080 --> 00:53:15.660
<v Ez Malone>--beating and bamming on it. Wasn't getting nothing out of it. And I said to him, I said, I wants to get so I can help you out. And I'm going to learn this thing through the help of the Lord. So there I was, upstairs in the room, just bamming on the guitar, trying to learn, day and night.
<v Ez Malone>——敲打着它。什么也没弹出来。我对他说，我说，我希望能帮上你的忙。我要在上帝的帮助下学会这个东西。所以我整天整夜在楼上的房间里拨弄吉他，试图学习。

00:53:15.660 --> 00:53:27.740
<v Ez Malone>And he encouraged me when he told me. He said, "When you learn how to play just three chords," sort of thing, "I'm going to take you to church and let you play," because I love going to church even now.
<v Ez Malone>当他告诉我时他鼓励我。他说：“当你学会怎么只弹三个和弦时，”那种事，“我要带你去教堂，让你弹，”因为直到现在我都爱去教堂。

00:53:27.740 --> 00:53:51.500
<v Ez Malone>So there I was in my bedroom, alone, sitting on my bed. And I was just a child. And I told Jesus. I said, "Lord," I said, "I want to play this thing to help my daddy out, because he's preaching your word. And he needs somebody to go with him." And all of a sudden out of nowhere, the Lord spoke to me in a solid voice from the inside. And he showed me this chord here, the E chord.
<v Ez Malone>所以在那儿，我独自在卧室里，坐在床上。我还是个孩子。我告诉耶稣。我说，“主啊，”我说，“我想弹这东西帮我爸爸，因为他在传你的道。他需要人陪他。”突然间，没有任何预兆，主以一种坚定的声音从里面跟我说话。他向我展示了这个和弦，E和弦。

00:53:51.500 --> 00:53:53.670
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:53:53.670 --> 00:54:05.870
<v Ez Malone>The Lord showed me. Never been to school for it. And I went downstairs, and I ran down there and showed it to my daddy. I said, "Dad, I believe I'm ready to play in church." And he'd say, "Well, let me hear what you sound like." And I didn't have but that one chord.
<v Ez Malone>主展示给我看了。我从未上过学。我跑下楼，跑到那儿向我爸爸展示。我说：“爸爸，我相信我准备好在教堂演奏了。”他说：“好吧，让我听听你弹得怎么样。”我只会那一个和弦。

00:54:05.870 --> 00:54:07.340
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:54:07.340 --> 00:54:24.630
<v Ez Malone>And he said, "Well, get two more chords, and I will take you to church. Learn two more notes, And I will take you to church." Oh, that excited me. So I ran back upstairs in my bedroom. And I told God, I said, "Lord, I need two more chords, just two more chords." And the Lord showed me the A.
<v Ez Malone>他说：“好吧，再学两个和弦，我就带你去教堂。再学两个音符，我就带你去教堂。”哦，那让我太兴奋了。于是我跑回楼上的卧室。我告诉上帝，我说：“主啊，我需要两个和弦，再要两个就行了。”主向我展示了A和弦。

00:54:24.630 --> 00:54:25.750
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:54:25.750 --> 00:54:27.310
<v Ez Malone>Then he showed me the B.
<v Ez Malone>然后他展示了B和弦。

