<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:54:39.320 --> 00:54:41.850
<v Ez Malone>He said, "That's good. Show me another one." I said--
<v Ez Malone>他说：“那很好。再展示一个给我看。”我说——

00:54:41.850 --> 00:54:43.200
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:54:43.200 --> 00:54:46.540
<v Ez Malone>He said, "That's good." He said, "Do you got one more?" I said--
<v Ez Malone>他说：“那很好。”他说：“你还有吗？”我说——

00:54:46.540 --> 00:54:47.690
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:54:47.690 --> 00:55:06.980
<v Ez Malone>So I went on like that there. And he took me to church and got me in front of a crowd of people. And it was so crowded in there, and I was so nervous, I couldn't hardly hold my legs still from shaking. And he said to the church, he said, "My son is going to make the guitar say 'Jesus.'"
<v Ez Malone>就这样我一直弹下去。他带我去教堂，把我带到一群人面前。里面人头攒动，我太紧张了，腿都在抖，根本停不下来。他对教堂的人说：“我儿子要让吉他叫出‘耶稣’。”

00:55:06.980 --> 00:55:20.730
<v Ez Malone>Now I looked at my mother. And I said, "Excuse me, mama. I need to talk to you." And she said, "What is it?" I said, "Well, now, which son is he talking about?" She said, "Son, you know he's talking about you."
<v Ez Malone>我看着母亲。我说：“对不起，妈。我得跟你说句话。”她说：“什么事？”我说：“嗯，现在，他说的是哪个儿子？”她说：“儿子，你知道他说的是你。”

00:55:20.730 --> 00:55:30.610
<v Ez Malone>I said, "Well, I can't make no guitar call 'Jesus,' you know?" She said, "Well, you know your dad don't play. So when you actually do it, you better learn something."
<v Ez Malone>我说：“嗯，我可没法让吉他叫‘耶稣’，你知道吧？”她说：“嗯，你知道你爸不会弹。所以当你真的做的时候，你最好学点什么。”

00:55:30.610 --> 00:55:51.920
<v Ez Malone>Get out there and hit the guitar, he hollared off. And like I said, being a minister, he would sing a song before he'd preach. And he said, "My son is going to make the guitar say Jesus." He said, "When I say 'Jesus," my son is going to make the guitar say 'Jesus.'" So he hauled off and looked at me. And he said, "Jesus." And I said--
<v Ez Malone>他大喊着让我出去弹吉他。就像我说的，作为牧师，他会在布道前唱首歌。他说：“我儿子要让吉他叫出耶稣。”他说：“当我喊‘耶稣’时，我儿子就要让吉他叫出‘耶稣’。”于是他站好看着我。他说：“耶稣。”我就说——

00:55:51.920 --> 00:55:54.990
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:55:54.990 --> 00:56:10.600
<v Ez Malone>And he stooped down before me and said, "Excuse me. You want me to take that guitar from you?" I said, "No, sir." He said, "I'm going to say it again. If you don't make it say Jesus, I'm going to take it from you." So he hollered off, man. He's scary, I'm telling you. And he said, "Jesus." And I said--
<v Ez Malone>他俯下身对我说：“对不起。你想让我把吉他收走吗？”我说：“不，先生。”他说：“我要再喊一次。如果你不让它叫耶稣，我就把它收走。”于是他大喊，天哪。他很吓人，我告诉你。他说：“耶稣。”我就说——

00:56:10.600 --> 00:56:13.560
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:56:13.560 --> 00:56:25.420
<v Ez Malone>He said, "Excuse me, church," and leaned down to me like this. "You want me to whip your tail?" I said, "No, sir. I don't want you to whip me tail. Please don't whip me. Please." Because when my father says he will whip you, he  will whip you.
<v Ez Malone>他说：“对不起，教堂，”然后这样俯身对我说。“你想让我鞭打你的尾巴（屁股）吗？”我说：“不，先生。我不想让你鞭打我。求求你别鞭打我。求你了。”因为当父亲说他会鞭打你时，他真的会鞭打你。

00:56:25.420 --> 00:56:34.460
<v Ez Malone>So I said, "Say it one more time. And I'm going to try to get it out this time." And he said it the third time. And when he said "Jesus," it came out of nowhere.
<v Ez Malone>所以我说：“再说一次。我这次会尽力做到的。”他说第三次。当他喊出“耶稣”时，它从虚无中蹦了出来。

00:56:34.460 --> 00:56:38.060
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:56:38.060 --> 00:56:49.860
<v Ez Malone>Like that there. And then he said, "I believe he can do a little bit better than that." I said, "No, I can't. I don't even know how I've done that," right? So he hollered off again. He said, "Jesus." And the next thing I remember,
<v Ez Malone>像那样。然后他说：“我相信他可以做得再好点。”我说：“不，我不行。我甚至不知道自己是怎么做到的，”对吧？于是他又大喊。他说：“耶稣。”接下来我记得的是，

00:56:49.860 --> 00:56:55.990
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:56:55.990 --> 00:57:03.550
<v Ez Malone>And that's how I learned to play. I learned through the miracle of Jesus Christ, and I learned through the fear for my father.
<v Ez Malone>我就是这样学会弹奏的。我是通过耶稣基督的奇迹学会的，我是通过对父亲的恐惧学会的。

00:57:03.550 --> 00:57:20.210
<v Ez Malone>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Ez Malone>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

00:57:20.210 --> 00:57:44.180
<v Carmen Delzell>EZ played the guitar with my son for the rest of the night while the women talked and laughed in the kitchen. I couldn't help wondering if my grandmother had heard EZ's story. It's funny how Jesus was so important to both of them. But she always told me when I was little that there were two heavens, one for black people and one for white. I don't think so.
<v Carmen Delzell>埃兹那天晚上剩下的时间一直和我儿子弹吉他，女人们在厨房里谈笑风生。我不禁好奇祖母有没有听到埃兹的故事。有趣的是，耶稣对他们俩都那么重要。但她小时候常告诉我，天堂有两个，一个是给黑人的，一个是给白人的。我不这么认为。

00:57:44.180 --> 00:57:56.800
<v Carmen Delzell>[MUSIC PLAYING - EZ MALONE]
<v Carmen Delzell>[音乐播放 - 埃兹·马隆]

